From 80a81de84f9b5d0674990bd38931a5eb4668588d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 03:43:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 314/314] gallium/pvr: asynchronous render submission, fences,
 no PR wait

- Renders are submitted without waiting: two slots each hold one render's
  transient memory (general and PDS arenas, control stream), the syncobj
  it signals and references to every resource it uses, and a slot is
  waited for only when reused. A CPU map submits the open render if it
  uses the resource and waits only for the last render that did; data
  sets are evicted only when idle.
- Real fences: flush returns a syncobj copy of the last render's fence and
  fence_finish waits on it (glFinish used to return at once).
- The fragment job no longer waits on the partial-render job, as the
  reference: the kernel keeps a context's fragment jobs in order, and the
  dependency cost a scheduler round trip between TA and 3D (firmware
  trace: 1039 -> 768 ticks).
- Drop trace-hook comments 0303 left behind in the Vulkan job code.

Multi-render scenes gain most (glmark2 desktop 52 -> 73, 146 -> 193).
